class.description:
Give the agent a set of [GoapAction]s it knows how to perform and a set of [GoapGoal]s it cares about, and it works out the rest: whenever it has no plan it asks [GoapPlanner] for one, then ticks the plan's actions in order until they run out or one of them fails.
[codeblock]
extends GoapAgent

func _ready():
    actions = [GetAxe.new(), ChopWood.new(), BuyAxe.new()]
    goals = [GatherWood.new(), Idle.new()]
    world_state = {&"has_axe": false, &"has_wood": false}
[/codeblock]
Each step the agent:
- plans, if it has no plan, picking the highest priority goal it can reach;
- re-checks the next action's [method GoapAction._is_valid] and preconditions, dropping the plan when the world no longer matches;
- calls [method GoapAction._enter] once, then [method GoapAction._tick] until it reports success or failure, then [method GoapAction._exit];
- on success, writes the action's effects into [member world_state] and moves on; on failure, drops the plan and starts over.
Nothing here is mandatory. [member process_callback] can be set to [constant PROCESS_CALLBACK_MANUAL] to drive the agent from your own code with [method update], and [GoapPlanner] can be used on its own if you would rather execute plans yourself.
[b]Note:[/b] The agent does not replan while a plan is running. Call [method request_plan] when something happens that should make it reconsider right away, such as taking damage.
